# Manifest of the gd test suites scripts/run-gd-tests.sh MUST find under
# cad/tests/gd/. Line format (v2, shared with pcb/tests/gd/EXPECTED_SUITES):
#
#     <filename> [assertions=N] [real-worker]
#
# - <filename>: exactly as it appears on disk. A suite going missing
#   (deleted, renamed, moved off the glob) or appearing unregistered is a
#   loud, named pre-flight failure in both directions.
# - assertions=N: the suite must report exactly N total assertions
#   (passed+failed). This is what makes `check(true); quit(0)` planted above
#   the real assertions FAIL instead of passing a bare `n_pass > 0` floor.
#   When a suite legitimately grows or shrinks, re-pin here in a deliberate,
#   reviewed own-commit — the same act as registering the suite.
# - real-worker: the suite's Results line must prove real_worker_used=true.
#   No cad suite uses it yet; the runner refuses the attribute until
#   cad/scripts/probe-worker-methods.py exists, because the attribute is a
#   claim about a live worker and an unprobed worker cannot back it.
#
# This file is deliberately NOT named test_*.gd (it must not match the
# runner's own `test_*.gd` glob) and NOT executable GDScript.

# Two controls (a normal middle-drag orbits; a received release stops the
# orbit) plus the repro (a LOST middle-button release must not strand the
# camera in orbit).
test_orbit_camera_stuck.gd assertions=3

# Reference meshes: a GLB built and written by the suite itself is loaded,
# converted from metres/Y-up to millimetres/Z-up with its 0.001 root scale
# composed, posed by the evaluation's 4x4, mounted shaded + outlined, cached
# against a pose change and re-read against a file change; plus path
# resolution, the missing-file report, the shared feature-edge extractor and
# reference-aware auto-framing.
test_reference_meshes.gd assertions=33

# The GUI "Import mesh…" action: the button and the scene-declared picker
# exist in both layouts, a pick appends exactly one refN = mesh("...") line
# with a path relative to the saved .mcad, the write lands on the SAME
# DocumentBuffer the paired text editor reads (real broker, real buffer), an
# evaluation follows on its own, a second import becomes ref2, and an unsaved
# document gets an absolute path plus an on-screen warning that survives
# Save-As and still resolves.
test_mesh_import.gd assertions=36

# Measuring a foreign mesh: a CSG plate with two plain through holes, one hole
# 1.9 mm from the outline, one drilled 30 degrees off the plate normal, a blind
# pocket and a convex boss, baked in-test and posed by a non-identity
# transform. Pins the propose half (segmentation, plane and cylinder fits,
# facet count, the inscribed-vs-circumscribed distinction, the axis of the
# tilted hole) and the verify half (colliders, refined centres in both frames,
# the pin that actually fits, through vs blind, a too-large gauge reporting
# contacts, the boss, a pixel-less probe, and the ray-grid fallback's limits).
test_mesh_measurement.gd assertions=56

# Failure and size handling for references: a truncated GLB, a text file
# wearing a .glb extension, a missing file, an unreadable format and an
# unresolvable relative path all mounted in ONE evaluation next to a good
# reference. Pins the status taxonomy and the reason naming the file, the
# wireframe marker drawn at the failed reference's own pose, the good
# reference and the rest of the scene surviving all four, the marker clearing
# on the next good evaluation, the three size ceilings (bytes refused before
# the parse, triangles refused after it, the outline budget degrading to
# shaded-only) with the measured numbers in the messages, and
# minerva_cad_references carrying references[i].status and its reason.
test_reference_failures.gd assertions=30

# Pointing at a reference: a two-box GLB built in-test, declared mm/Z-up so the
# frame conversion is the identity and the suite is about WHICH node was hit.
# Pins the node inventory and the scene-declared sidebar rows, a click in the
# top pane picking the nearer of two bodies and reporting its surface point in
# both frames, the MCP readback (get_selected_reference / select_reference,
# including a miss being an error and a flat face reporting no hole), the
# cad/point anchor validating, resolving, moving with a re-posed reference by
# the projected pixel displacement and going stale — not crashing — when the
# reference leaves the document, and the two selections coexisting: the picker
# is a plain Node that only ever sees input the edge overlay did not take.
test_reference_selection.gd assertions=41
